gistered t0-baseline artifact on item 3169 containing one recorded result per criterion-id.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. All eight criterion-ids (AC1..AC8) have a recorded exit code.\\n2. AC8-full-suite-green records a passing baseline; if it does not, report the pre-existing failures and STOP \\u2014 the tree is not green before work starts.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Re-read the registered artifact and confirm eight entries are present.\",\"handoff\":\"Report the baseline table (criterion-id, exit code, pass/fail) and flag any criterion whose baseline differs from its expected-baseline.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"low\",\"is_bookend\":true,\"bookend_type\":\"t0-baseline\"},{\"id\":\"T1\",\"title\":\"Extract the full-text search engine from server.py into a FastMCP-free backlog_core/search.py\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T15:42:35.265118+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T22:00:22.600525+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Problem 1 in the architect spec is that one algorithm is trapped above the layer that needs it. The search engine lives in backlog_core/server.py, which imports FastMCP, so backlog_core/operations.py cannot reach it. This task is a pure relocation \\u2014 no logic is rewritten, no behaviour changes, no new function is added (T2 adds those). Spec reference: \\u00a74.1 and \\u00a72.2.\",\"objective\":\"Relocate the existing tokenizer, boolean-query parser, predicate AST, and snippet helpers out of the FastMCP server module into a new pure module that operations.py can import, with zero behaviour change.\",\"requirements\":\"1. Create `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/search.py`.\\n2. Move these symbols out of `backlog_core/server.py` into it, renaming exactly the two the spec makes public and leaving the rest private:\\n   - `_tokenize_search` (server.py:391) -> public `tokenize_search(query: str) -> list[str]`\\n   - `_apply_search_filter` (server.py:516) -> public `apply_search_filter(items: list[dict[str, str | bool]], query: str) -> list[dict[str, str | bool]]`\\n   - stay private, moved verbatim: `_SearchParser` (426), `_Predicate` (318), `_TermPred` (338), `_AndPred` (348), `_OrPred` (359), `_NotPred` (370), `_TruePred` (379), `_build_haystack` (252), `_item_matches_term` (261), `_SEARCH_FIELDS` (194), `_parse_body_sections` (570), `_make_snippet` (599), `_make_snippet_parts` (623), `_format_match_text` (668), `_META_FIELDS` (699), `_SNIPPET_WINDOW` (564), `_DEFAULT_SNIPPET_CONTEXT` (567).\\n3. Delete the moved definitions from `server.py` and import them back from `backlog_core.search`. `server.py`'s match_context annotation layer stays in `server.py` and keeps calling the moved snippet helpers via the new import.\\n4. Keep every call site in `server.py` working \\u2014 in particular `_apply_search_filter(all_items, search)` at server.py:2166 becomes a call to the imported `apply_search_filter` (T4 moves this call into operations.list_items; do NOT move it here).\\n5. Add a module docstring stating the layering invariant: search.py operates on the `list[dict[str, str | bool]]` shape produced by `operations.py::_build_list_entry` and must never import FastMCP or MCP types.\",\"constraints\":\"- No behaviour change. Do not fix, simplify, optimise, or re-type the moved code \\u2014 a relocation diff only.\\n- `search.py` MUST NOT import `fastmcp` or `mcp` (this is what makes it importable from operations.py).\\n- Do not add `find_content_duplicates`, `build_concept_query`, `ContentDuplicateMatch`, or `DuplicateCheckStatus` here \\u2014 that is T2.\\n- Do not touch `operations.py`, `parsing.py`, `models.py`, or any test file in this task.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"- Created: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/search.py`\\n- Modified: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. `backlog_core/search.py` exists and defines all 19 symbols listed in Requirement 2.\\n2. `tokenize_search` and `apply_search_filter` are public (no leading underscore); the other 17 keep their leading underscore.\\n3. `grep -nE '^[[:space:]]*(from|import)[[:space:]]+(fastmcp|mcp)([.[:space:]]|$)' plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/search.py` returns nothing (structured criterion AC7).\\n4. No definition listed in Requirement 2 remains defined in `server.py` \\u2014 each is imported instead.\\n5. The full development-harness suite passes unchanged (structured criterion AC8). Because this is a relocation, ZERO existing tests should need editing; if any test needs a change, the relocation was not behaviour-preserving \\u2014 stop and report rather than editing the test.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. `cd /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills && uv run pytest plugins/development-harness -q`\\n2. `cd /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills && ! grep -nE '^[[:space:]]*(from|import)[[:space:]]+(fastmcp|mcp)([.[:space:]]|$)' plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/search.py`\\n3. `cd /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills && uv run python -c \\\"import backlog_core.search as s; print(s.tokenize_search('a OR b'))\\\"` \\u2014 proves the module imports standalone without the FastMCP server.\\n4. `cd /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills && git diff --stat plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \\u2014 the diff should be dominated by deletions plus one import block.\\n5. `git add plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/search.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` then `git commit -m \\\"refactor(backlog_core): extract full-text search engine into FastMCP-free search module\\\"`\",\"context_notes\":\"CoVe \\u2014 key claims to verify before committing:\\n- Claim: