ps working for existing tests \\u2014 marked with inline `noqa: F401`-equivalent comments since ruff's redundant-self-alias re-export idiom is only honoured in `__init__.py`), and `apply_search_filter as _apply_search_filter` / `tokenize_search as _tokenize_search`.\\n\\nNo test file was touched (verified via `git status --short` on tests/ and sam_schema/tests/ before commit).\\n\\nVerification:\\n- `grep -nE '^[[:space:]]*(from|import)[[:space:]]+(fastmcp|mcp)([.[:space:]]|$)' backlog_core/search.py` \\u2192 no matches (AC7 satisfied).\\n- `PYTHONPATH=plugins/development-harness uv run python -c \\\"import backlog_core.search as s; print(s.tokenize_search('a OR b'))\\\"` \\u2192 succeeds standalone.\\n- `git diff --stat backlog_core/server.py` \\u2192 12 insertions, 464 deletions (dominated by deletions + one import block).\\n- `uv run ruff check backlog_core/search.py backlog_core/server.py` \\u2192 all checks passed.\\n- Full suite `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness -q`: first run showed 4 failures (test_artifact_provider_local, 2x test_network_guard, test_github_sync_provider); isolated each \\u2014 3 were xdist worker-ordering flakiness (pass individually and on a clean re-run), and the 4th (`test_github_content_provider_replay_preserves_concurrent_remote_revision`) reproduces identically on the pre-change baseline (verified via `git stash`), confirming it is a pre-existing, unrelated failure on this branch (likely tied to the already-committed sync-engine retry-classification work), not caused by this relocation. A second full run showed only that one pre-existing failure: 5310 passed, 1 failed (pre-existing), 42 skipped, 5 xfailed.\\n\\nCommitted as 44873fa9c: \\\"refactor(backlog_core): extract full-text search engine into FastMCP-free search module\\\" \\u2014 pre-commit hooks (ruff lint/format, ty check, conventional-commit) all passed.\",\"handoff\":\"Report: the symbol inventory moved, the server.py import block added, confirmation that no test file was touched, and the pytest result.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"medium\"},{\"id\":\"T2\",\"title\":\"Add the content-duplicate primitives to backlog_core/search.py\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T1\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T15:42:35.265145+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T22:21:50.811924+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Adds the content-matching primitive that replaces character-sequence title matching. Purely additive \\u2014 no existing caller changes in this task, so the tree and the whole suite stay green throughout. Spec reference: \\u00a74.1 (signatures), \\u00a76.2 and \\u00a76.3 (type contracts), ADR-004 (why token overlap, not edit distance).\",\"objective\":\"Add DuplicateCheckStatus, ContentDuplicateMatch, build_concept_query, and find_content_duplicates to the extracted search module as a pure addition that nothing yet consumes.\",\"requirements\":\"1. Add to `backlog_core/search.py`, using these signatures verbatim from spec \\u00a74.1:\\n```python\\nclass DuplicateCheckStatus(StrEnum):\\n    DUPLICATE_FOUND = \\\"duplicate_found\\\"\\n    NO_DUPLICATE = \\\"no_duplicate\\\"\\n    COULD_NOT_VERIFY = \\\"could_not_verify\\\"\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\\nclass ContentDuplicateMatch:\\n    title: str\\n    item_ref: str          # \\\"#3141\\\" or \\\"bd-a3f8\\\" \\u2014 never a bare file path\\n    matched_field: str     # e.g. \\\"title\\\", \\\"body:acceptance-criteria\\\"\\n    snippet: str           # ~120-char window around the match\\n    match_count: int       # number of concept-query terms this candidate matched\\n\\n\\ndef build_concept_query(title: str, description: str, *, max_concepts: int = 4) -> str: ...\\n\\n\\ndef find_content_duplicates(\\n    title: str,\\n    description: str,\\n    candidates: list[dict[str, str | bool]],\\n    *,\\n    max_results: int = 5,\\n) -> list[ContentDuplicateMatch]: ...\\n```\\n2. `build_concept_query` builds an OR query from significant words across title + description, dropping a small embedded stopword set and tokens under a minimum length, and returns `\\\"\\\"` when no usable concept remains. This mirrors the manual concept extraction that `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` Step 3 already prescribes (\\\"extract 2 to 4 key concepts ... build {c1} OR {c2} OR {c3}\\\").\\n3. `find_content_duplicates` calls `build_concept_query`, filters `candidates` through the existing `apply_search_filter`, ranks survivors by number of matched concept terms descending, and projects the top `max_results` into `ContentDuplicateMatch` \\u2014 reusing the moved `_make_snippet_parts` for the `snippet` field. Returns `[]` when the query is empty or nothing matches.\\n4. Preserve the one behaviour the old algorithm had that still matters: candidates flagged skip/done are excluded, and candidates with an empty title are skipped.\\n5. `item_ref` precedence (spec \\u00a76.2 invariant): the candidate's issue reference when set, else its `reference` field \\u2014 the same precedence `add_item`'s own return dict already uses. Never a bare file path, never empty.\",\"constraints\":\"- `search.py` still must not import `fastmcp`/`mcp`, and must not import `operations.py` (that would invert the layering).\\n- Use `StrEnum` and `@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)` exactly as specified \\u2014 do not substitute Pydantic, NamedTuple, or a plain class.\\n- Do not introduce a similarity threshold constant. Ranking is by `match_count`, deliberately not by a scalar cliff (spec DO-5 rationale).\\n- Do not add `difflib` or any new third-party dependency.\\n- Do not modify `operations.py`, `models.py`, `parsing.py`, or `server.py` in this task.\\n- Do not introduce a `TypedDict` for the candidate shape \\u2014 spec \\u00a76.4 flags this as deliberately deferred.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"- Modified: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/search.py`\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. All four symbols exist with the exact signatures in Requirement 1, including keyword-only `max_concepts` and `max_results` and their defaults 4 and 5.\\n2. `ContentDuplicateMatch` is frozen and slotted; mutating a field raises.\\n3. `build_concept_query(\\\"\\\", \\\"\\\")` returns `\\\"\\\"`, and `find_content_duplicates` returns `[]` for an empty query.\\n4. `find_content_duplicates` never returns more than `max_results` items, and results are ordered by `match_count` descending.\\n5. `ty` (or the project's configured type checker) reports no new errors on `search.py`; no `Any`, no `cast()`, no bare `object` is introduced (spec \\u00a76.4).\\n6. The full suite still passes \\u2014 this task is additive and must break nothing (structured criterion AC8).\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. `cd /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills && uv run pytest plugins/development-harness -q`\\n2. `cd /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills && uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/search.py` (or the project's configured checker; report which was used).\\n3. Ad-hoc proof the incident pair now matches \\u2014 run `find_content_duplicates` with title \\\"Agent `tools:` frontmatter drifts from MCP server tool lists with no enforcement and silent failure in both directions\\\" against a candidate list containing an entry titled \\\"CI check for drift between MCP server tool lists and agent frontmatter `tools:` entries\\\" and confirm a non-empty result. T5 pins this as a permanent test; this step is the immediate proof the algorithm actually solves the reported defect.\\n4. `git add plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/search.py` then `git commit -m \\\"feat(backlog_core): add content-based duplicate matching primitives to search module\\\"`\",\"context_notes\":\"CoVe \\u2014 this task carries real accuracy risk because a wrong ranking heuristic silently under- or over-matches. Verify before committing:\\n- Claim: the incident pair from #3169 matches. Question: does verification step 3 return a non-empty list? Evidence: the actual output. If it does not, the concept extraction or stopword set is wrong \\u2014 fix it here, do not defer to T5.\\n- Claim: genuinely unrelated items do not match. Question: do two real, unrelated resolved backlog items in the same subsystem produce a match? Evidence: run the same ad-hoc call with a deliberately unrelated pair and show the empty result. AC5's pinned corpus is built in T5, but a spot check here catches a runaway stopword set early.\\n- Claim: `item_ref` is never a file path. Question: what does `find_content_duplicates` emit for a candidate whose entry has no issue number? Evidence: the emitted value, which must be the `reference` field.\\nRevision rule: if either matching check fails, tune `build_concept_query` (stopwords, minimum token length, max_concepts) and re-run both \\u2014 never relax the non-match check to make the match check pass.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"medium\"},{\"id\":\"T3\",\"title\":\"Replace title-fuzzy duplicate detection with the tri-state content check and delete the old algorithm\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T2\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"high\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T15:42:35.265170+00:00\",\"started\":\"2026-08-28T22:30:34.825765+00:00\",\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T23:13:23.293254+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"This is the atomic swap. models.py, operations.py, and parsing.py must change together \\u2014 deleting `find_fuzzy_duplicates` while `operations.py:66` still imports it, or reshaping `DuplicateItemError` while its only raise site still passes tuples, leaves the tree broken. Do all three in this one task. Test files are NOT updated here; the suite will be red between this task and T5/T6, which is expected and is why those two tasks exist. Spec reference: \\u00a74.2, \\u00a74.3, ADR-002, ADR-003, ADR-004, ADR-005.\",\"objective\":\"Swap operations.py's write-time gate onto find_content_duplicates via a tri-state classifier, reshape DuplicateItemError to carry actionable matches, and remove find_fuzzy_duplicates and FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD entirely.\",\"requirements\":\"1. `backlog_core/models.py`: redefine `DuplicateItemError` (currently models.py:561) to `def __init__(self, duplicates: list[ContentDuplicateMatch]) -> None`. Build the message from `item_ref` and `title` \\u2014 e.g. `'\\\"{title}\\\" ({item_ref})'`. Drop the percentage entirely; do not re-derive a fake percentage from `match_count` (spec \\u00a74.3).\\n2. `backlog_core/models.py`: delete `FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD` (models.py:422).\\n3. `backlog_core/parsing.py`: delete `find_fuzzy_duplicates` (parsing.py:536), its `__all__` entry (parsing.py:69), and its now-unused `FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD` import (parsing.py:38) and `difflib` import if nothing else in the file uses it.\\n4. `backlog_core/operations.py`: remove the `find_fuzzy_duplicates` import (operations.py:66) and add the `backlog_core.search` imports.\\n5. `backlog_core/operations.py`: add the private classifier, verbatim signature from spec \\u00a74.2:\\n```python\\ndef _classify_duplicate_check(\\n    title: str, description: str, repo: str, out: Output\\n) -> tuple[DuplicateCheckStatus, list[ContentDuplicateMatch]]: ...\\n```\\n   It reads the local cache via `_build_list_entry(item, {})` over `backend.list_work_items()`, scores with `find_content_duplicates()`, and implements exactly this decision table (spec \\u00a74.2):\\n   | Local match? | Backend is `SyncProvider`? | Refresh outcome | Result |\\n   |---|---|---|---|\\n   | Yes | \\u2014 | \\u2014 | `DUPLICATE_FOUND` |\\n   | No | No (SQLite/Memory/Beads) | not attempted | `NO_DUPLICATE` |\\n   | No | Yes | succeeds, still no match | `NO_DUPLICATE` |\\n   | No | Yes | succeeds, now matches | `DUPLICATE_FOUND` |\\n   | No | Yes | raises `(GithubException, BacklogError)` | `COULD_NOT_VERIFY`, warning appended to `out` |\\n   The refresh is one bounded incremental call: `refresh_local_cache_from_github(repo=repo, output=out, full_refresh=False)`. Catch `(GithubException, BacklogError)` \\u2014 the same tuple `_try_create_github_issue` already catches in this file. Never propagate a refresh failure.\\n6. `backlog_core/operations.py`: rewrite `_check_for_duplicates` (operations.py:1341) as a thin wrapper, verbatim from spec \\u00a74.2:\\n```python\\ndef _check_for_duplicates(\\n    title: str, description: str, force: bool, repo: str, out: Output\\n) -> None:\\n    if force:\\n        return\\n    status, matches = _classify_duplicate_check(title, description, repo, out)\\n    match status:\\n        case DuplicateCheckStatus.DUPLICATE_FOUND:\\n            raise DuplicateItemError(matches)\\n        case DuplicateCheckStatus.NO_DUPLICATE | DuplicateCheckStatus.COULD_NOT_VERIFY:\\n            return\\n```\\n7. `backlog_core/operations.py`: update the call site at operations.py:1503 from `_check_for_duplicates(title, force)` to `_check_for_duplicates(title, description, force, repo, out)`. `add_item`'s own signature and contract do not change.\\n8. Verify (do not modify) that the SQLite, Memory, and Beads backends need no change: none is a `SyncProvider`, so the refresh branch is never reached for them. State this explicitly in the handoff.\",\"constraints\":\"- `find_fuzzy_duplicates` is REMOVED, not retained as a fallback and not deprecated (ADR-004). No compatibility shim, no union type accepting the old tuple shape (ADR-005).\\n- The write-time gate stays inside `add_item` and stays unconditional (ADR-002). Do not move it, do not add a second gate, and do not add a new public pre-check function (spec \\u00a74.4 cuts it per YAGNI).\\n- `COULD_NOT_VERIFY` MUST NOT raise and MUST NOT block creation \\u2014 the item is still created and a warning reaches the caller through `Output.warnings`. A new rejection class would violate AC5.\\n- The refresh runs ONLY when no local match was found AND the backend is a `SyncProvider` (ADR-003). Never refresh on the path that already found a match, and never for native-storage backends.\\n- `force=True` keeps meaning \\\"skip the check entirely\\\" (spec \\u00a74.2, OQ-5 resolved). Do not redefine it.\\n- Use `match`/`case`, not an if/elif chain, for the status dispatch (spec \\u00a74.2, Stage 1 review compliance).\\n- Both new functions stay private. Do not export them.\\n- Do not edit any test file in this task.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"- Modified: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py`\\n- Modified: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/parsing.py`\\n- Modified: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py`\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. `grep -rn --include='*.py' -e find_fuzzy_duplicates -e FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD plugins/development-harness` returns nothing outside test files (structured criterion AC6 covers the full removal once T5 deletes the tests).\\n2. `_classify_duplicate_check` and `_check_for_duplicates` have exactly the signatures in Requirements 5 and 6.\\n3. `_check_for_duplicates` dispatches with `match status:`, and the `COULD_NOT_VERIFY` arm returns without raising.\\n4. `refresh_local_cache_from_github` is called on exactly one code path in `_classify_duplicate_check`, guarded by both \\\"no local match\\\" and `isinstance(backend, SyncProvider)`.\\n5. `DuplicateItemError.__init__` accepts `list[ContentDuplicateMatch]`; its message contains `item_ref` and contains no percentage.\\n6. Production code imports and type-checks cleanly: `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/` reports no n